            <ArticleTitle>Iopamidol compared with Conray in peripheral angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>549-52</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In patients with arteriosclerotic disease in the legs, peripheral angiography was performed double blind with the non-ionic contrast medium Iopamidol and the ionic medium iothalamate meglumine (Conray 60). Iopamidol caused less subjective adverse effects and less changes in blood pressure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
